The response travels back through the application server → web server → load balancer → the internet → your browser. Your browser receives the HTML, renders the DOM, loads CSS and JavaScript, and displays the Google homepage — all in a fraction of a second.

What looks like a trivial keystroke is actually a beautifully orchestrated symphony of protocols, encryption, routing, and distributed computing working in perfect unison.

